{'symbol': 'AWK', 'date': '2022-08-12 11:35:00', 'title': 'MISSOURI AMERICAN WATER INVESTS $5 MILLION TO REPLACE 1930S WATER MAINS IN AFFTON', 'text': 'AFFTON, MO.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--MISSOURI AMERICAN WATER WILL REPLACE NEARLY 8,000 FEET (APPROXIMATELY 1.5 MILES) OF AGING WATER MAIN IN AFFTON, MO STARTING THIS SUMMER. THE COMPANY IS UPGRADING THE AGING 8- AND 12-INCH CAST-IRON WATER MAINS THAT WERE INSTALLED IN THE 1930S WITH NEW 12-INCH AND 16-INCH DUCTILE IRON MAINS ALONG THE FOLLOWING STREETS: GRAVOIS ROAD FROM TESSON FERRY ROAD TO NEW HAMPSHIRE AVENUE NEW HAMPSHIRE AVENUE FROM GRAVOIS ROAD TO WEBER ROAD WEBER ROAD FROM VALCOUR AVENUE TO GRA'}